      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(signal): expose mention facts in inbound context",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSignal group mention gating now has native mention metadata available, but the delivered-turn decision facts are only visible inside the Signal monitor. Downstream prompt/tool context cannot inspect whether the inbound group message had native mention metadata, whether `requireMention` was enforced for that delivered turn, or which mention path matched the bot. That makes native-only group behavior hard to debug and forces consumers to infer channel-specific facts from text.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Exposes Signal mention-gating facts on the generic inbound message context.\n- Adds `CanDetectMention`, `HasAnyMention`, `EffectiveWasMentioned`, `MentionShouldSkip`, and `MentionSource` for delivered native/text mention decisions, while reusing the existing canonical `GroupRequireMention` field.\n- Keeps the Signal mention source literal typed so SDK/context consumers can rely on `\"native\"` vs `\"mention_pattern\"`.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is stacked after #96738 (`fix(signal): detect native bot mentions in group gating`). Until #96738 lands, this PR's diff will include that dependency.\n\n## Production impact\n\nNo new outbound behavior. This only makes already-computed delivered-turn mention gating facts inspectable by prompts, tests, and plugin/channel contracts. Skipped Signal turns still return before prompt/tool context is built, so this PR intentionally does not expose a public skipped-turn context field.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused Signal/channel tests cover native mention facts being projected into inbound context:\n  `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/channels/inbound-event/context.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts`\n- Plugin SDK runtime mock tests cover `Mention*` parity with production inbound context.\n- Broader affected-context regression suite passed:\n  `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/openclaw-tools.plugin-context.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner-utils.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/inbound-meta.test.ts extensions/memory-core/index.test.ts extensions/memory-core/src/tools.citations.test.ts src/channels/inbound-event/context.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts`\n- Focused SDK mock test passed:\n  `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/plugin-sdk/test-helpers/plugin-runtime-mock.test.ts`\n- Plugin SDK API check passed:\n  `pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check`\n- Production TypeScript check passed:\n  `pnpm tsgo:prod`\n\n### Redacted Runtime Proof\n\nThe current-head terminal proof is in the Evidence update below. Earlier local proof from an older head was removed from this body to avoid stale field names and stale commit evidence.\n\n### Operational Signal group evidence (2026-06-26)\n\nA private Signal group smoke was run after a production config hotfix that kept the group-bound agent responding without changing Docker permissions. The private runtime intentionally stayed on its deployed OpenClaw release instead of being advanced to this PR stack today; the facts below are operational evidence for the real Signal group route, not an additional claim that this PR head is live-deployed.\n\nSanitized facts:\n\n- `openclaw config validate` against `/run/user/1000/openclaw/openclaw.json`: `valid=true`, exit `0`.\n- `openclaw-gateway.service`: `active/running`, `NRestarts=0`.\n- A native Signal mention from a group participant produced an outbound group reply; the journal recorded `delivered reply to group` at `2026-06-26T13:03:19+02:00`.\n- Latest group-bound Signal session metadata for the private family agent: `systemSent=true`, `abortedLastRun=false`.\n- Journal after the smoke: `Failed to inspect sandbox image` count `0`.\n\nDeployment note: the private runtime is not being upgraded to this stack today because that would mix the PR validation with an unrelated Docker sandbox repair. The long-term Docker/rootless sandbox fix is being tracked separately.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/plugin-sdk/test-helpers/plugin-runtime-mock.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/channels/inbound-event/context.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/openclaw-tools.plugin-context.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner-utils.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/inbound-meta.test.ts extensions/memory-core/index.test.ts extensions/memory-core/src/tools.citations.test.ts src/channels/inbound-event/context.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts`\n- `pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check`\n- `pnpm tsgo:prod`\n\n### Evidence update\n\nCurrent-head proof on `codex/signal-mention-facts-context` (`4bcda17af9`):\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/channels/inbound-event/context.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/test-helpers/plugin-runtime-mock.test.ts\n[test] passed 3 Vitest shards in 15.32s\n\n$ node --max-old-space-size=8192 --import tsx scripts/generate-plugin-sdk-api-baseline.ts --check\nOK docs/.generated/plugin-sdk-api-baseline.sha256\n\n$ git diff --check\n# passed with no output\n```\n\nCurrent-head terminal proof at the real Signal event-handler boundary. The temporary harness imported production `createSignalEventHandler`, used the production native mention resolver and mention decision helper, and captured the `dispatchInboundMessage` boundary through the channel contract testing helper. The harness used only synthetic/redacted identifiers and was not committed.\n\n```text\n$ OC_PROOF_HEAD=4bcda17af9 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/src/monitor/signal-mention-context-proof.test.ts --silent=false --reporter=verbose\nruntime-proof:environment\n{\n  \"pr\": 96862,\n  \"head\": \"4bcda17af9\",\n  \"boundary\": [\n    \"dispatchInboundMessage\",\n    \"runtime-drop/pending-history\"\n  ],\n  \"privacy\": \"all ids, phone numbers, participant names, group ids, and message bodies are synthetic\"\n}\n\nruntime-proof:#96862 native bot mention dispatchInboundMessage context\n{\n  \"Body\": \"<redacted-rendered-bot-mention-message>\",\n  \"CanDetectMention\": true,\n  \"WasMentioned\": true,\n  \"HasAnyMention\": true,\n  \"GroupRequireMention\": true,\n  \"EffectiveWasMentioned\": true,\n  \"MentionShouldSkip\": false,\n  \"MentionSource\": \"native\"\n}\n\nruntime-proof:#96862 non-bot native mention runtime drop boundary\n{\n  \"dispatchInboundMessageCalled\": false,\n  \"skipBoundaryObserved\": true,\n  \"pendingHistoryCount\": 1,\n  \"pendingHistoryBody\": \"<redacted-rendered-non-bot-mention-message>\",\n  \"nativeFacts\": {\n    \"canDetectMention\": true,\n    \"hasAnyMention\": true,\n    \"mentionsBot\": false\n  },\n  \"mentionDecision\": {\n    \"effectiveWasMentioned\": false,\n    \"mentionShouldSkip\": true\n  }\n}\n\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  1 passed (1)\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 8.65s\n```\n\nInspectable assertions covered:\n\n- Native Signal bot mention reaches the delivered `dispatchInboundMessage` context with:\n  `CanDetectMention=true`, `WasMentioned=true`, `HasAnyMention=true`,\n  `GroupRequireMention=true`, `EffectiveWasMentioned=true`,\n  `MentionShouldSkip=false`, `MentionSource=\"native\"`.\n- Native Signal mention of another participant does not dispatch; it is skipped into pending group history with the same production mention decision reporting `mentionShouldSkip=true`.\n- `MsgContext.WasMentioned` remains the effective mention-gating result for delivered Signal turns.\n- Existing `GroupRequireMention` remains the canonical require-mention policy field; the transient\n  `RequireMention` alias was removed after review.\n- `createPluginRuntimeMock` mirrors both `GroupRequireMention` and `MentionShouldSkip`.\n\nNo private Signal identifiers, phone numbers, participant names, group ids, or message bodies are used in this proof.\n",
